A post-mortum, "it went amazingly well" [0] update.

I've just received results of questionaries that were filled by
attendees. There were 10 presenatation during 2 days of conference.

The SELinux presentation took second place in general classification
which is IMO very good result. It is worth mentioning that it was best
ranked in "usefulness" (4.57 points avg) which shows that SELinux is
seen as possibly useful technology. The notes for "preparation"
and "presentation" were accordingly 4.60 and 4.53 avg. which made the
final result be (4.57+4.60+4.53)/3=3D4.57 (1st place presenation got 4.67
final avg., 3rd one got 4.44). [1]

So if you notoice dozens of people from Poland asking around strange
SELinux-related question - then you'll know who to blame :-)

Thanks Russell for all your help and patience,
thank You all who put your effort into SELinux

					Grzegorz B. Prokopski

